  m_Name: PY_10_MIXED
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: PY_10_MIXED
  language: 1
  topic: Mixed
  difficulty: 1
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Fill in the condition so the loop prints only the even numbers in
    nums.
  code: "for n in nums:\n    if ____:\n        print(n)"
  answerFormat: 2
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: n % 2 == 0
  runTests:
  - setup: 'nums = [3, 4, 7, 10]'
    expectedOutput: '4

      10'
  - setup: 'nums = [2, 5]'
    expectedOutput: 2
  - setup: 'nums = [1, 3]'
    expectedOutput: 
  explanation: n % 2 is the remainder after dividing by 2. Even numbers have remainder
    0, so n % 2 == 0 prints 4 and 10 for [3, 4, 7, 10]. n / 2 would divide instead,
    and n % 2 == 1 would pick the odd numbers.
  hint: The % operator gives the remainder of a division.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: Even numbers leave no remainder when divided by 2. Use the
    remainder operator and compare with ==.
